    "narrative": "For the May 19th slate, the Austin Waves lineup centers on **Kyle Tucker**, whose 74.01 efficiency score makes him our premier start. Facing Griffin Canning, **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a favorable matchup against an average starter in a park that doesn't hinder his elite power-speed profile. Similarly, **Sam Antonacci** (66.39) and **Josh Jung** (66.28) anchor our infield projections. **Sam Antonacci** capitalizes on the favorable xERA of Bryce Miller, while **Josh Jung** gets a significant boost from park factors and a manageable matchup against Sammy Peralta, though we must keep a close eye on the 45% rain risk hovering over his contest.\n\nBeyond our top tier, **Andy Pages** (59.07) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (61.16) provide steady production despite some pitching resistance. The most difficult decision today involved the final roster spot; **Nolan Schanuel** was the strongest consideration for the bench with a 55.83 score, but he narrowly missed the cut behind the optimizer\u2019s preference for **Jackson Merrill**\u2019s higher upside against Emmet Sheehan. While **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Miguel Vargas** all land in the mid-to-high 50s, they remain solid starts even against tougher arms like Nolan McLean and Griffin Jax. Conversely, **Nasim Nunez** was excluded despite his utility, falling below our 40.0 floor due to a bottom-of-the-order assignment that suppresses his counting stat potential. We are monitoring all \"Lineup Pending\" statuses, as any drastic shifts in batting order for **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** or **Gunnar Henderson** could necessitate a recalibration of our expected output for the day.",
